or_status":null,"result":"I'm approving PKT-0148. It's an investigate packet, so it wasn't meant to make x2t faster. The rule that rejects a performance change for zero gain doesn't apply here. What it had to deliver was a measured, honest diagnosis, and it does.\n\n**Goal**\n- `x2t-r3.md` records the oracle run. `DIAG-x2t.md` is now round 3, with `goals_hash: dcb03039`, `diagnosed_by` set, and a YAML plan under `## Initial packet plan` that is ordered by the time each stage costs users.\n- **Journey coverage:** six journeys have a stage owned by x2t, and every one is accounted for. The `x2t` stage (convert-docx-pdf and save) is under `covers`. The `server-open-x2t` stage (the four open journeys) is under `not_covered`, with a measured reason: that conversion never starts the JS engine, and it is only 3–8% of each journey.\n- **Round 2 judged honestly:** the diagnosis counts round 2 as 0 ms gained for users. `external/core` is still identical to `core.base`, so both sides ran the same binary. The work that was correct but changed no x2t code (PKT-0138, PKT-0108) is counted as not delivered, as the goal requires.\n\n**Contract and budget**\n- No source code changed, and `external/core` has no diff.\n- Four files and about 190 diff lines, well within the limits.\n- `DIAG-x2t-b.md` didn't exist, so there was nothing to delete.\n\n**Packet records**\n- The executor log is filled in, and the friction line is present and well formed.\n- No follow-ups were requested and `.theseus/spawn/` is empty, which is consistent.\n- PKT-0147 is marked superseded in the diagnosis; discarding it is left to the factory.\n\n**Plan**\n- P2 depends on the outcome of PKT-0143, which is already queued. It has a stop rule (at least 0.3 s saved) and falls back to one process per task.\n- It names the main risk, state leaking between documents in a reused engine, and requires the oracle to run several documents through one process to check for it.\n- `convert-docx-pdf.md` asks the next diagnosis to split that journey's x2t step into its three sub-steps. The diagnosis cites PKT-0108's split, which answers that.\n\n**Minor points (not blocking)**\n- The browser timings in `x2t-r3.md` don't match the factory's oracle output, which came from a different run. Both look like VM noise, and neither is used as evidence of a gain.\n- Because stage ids repeat across journeys, `covers: [x2t]` can't tell the convert journey from the save journey. The executor noted this method gap as a lesson for the Atlas.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE round-3 diagnosis is complete, honest about round 2's zero gain, covers every x2t journey stage, and its plan has a measured go/no-go condition","ttft_ms":2594,"type":"result","duration_ms":24982,"uuid":"de401fab-6d6e-450a-b823-b6bfdcc99de6","ttft_stream_ms":1955,"time_to_request_ms":315,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":182,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":24,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":9,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":9,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":8,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":20,"query_setup":4,"auto_mode_context_wait":7,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":17,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":5,"request_build":8},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":36,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":149,"time_to_request_major_faults":17,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":210,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":216,"process_anon_mib_result":131,"process_peak_rss_mib":244,"process_cpu_ms_turn":1050,"process_wall_ms_turn":24981,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":330,"process_wall_ms_streaming":15317,"main_stream_count":5,"main_stream_event_count":288,"main_stream_chunk_count":97,"process_turn_states":{"main_stream":{"cpu_ms":330,"wall_ms":15317,"entries":5},"tool":{"cpu_ms":73,"wall_ms":201,"entries":3},"first_event_wait":{"cpu_ms":394,"wall_ms"